Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||06:43 PM||||<BR>ok what would happen if I used a V6 Fuel pump on my duke? would the pump burn up @ 15-20 psi? also what would a solid dog bone & motor mounts do? other than the comfort level of the car would I do damage to the car by mounting it solid to the cradle? and the last question Where can I get a Steel crank for the duke at? Thanks so much for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-04-2000||07:24 PM||||You want solid cradle mounts Not solid motor mounts. Solid motor mounts will break things.<P>The V6 pump will likely give the TBI a caniption. The V6 pump puts out way more than the TBI fuel pressure regulator is likely to handle right.<P>I don't know of anyplace that does steel cranks for these. Maybe the people who do the $12,000 super duty but they're about it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||baldlobo||10-04-2000||08:21 PM||||isn't it Kansas Racing Products at <A HREF="http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/</A>  and they make Scat billet crankshafts fully machined||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||08:44 PM|||| I'll have ti give them a call tomorow and see about the Billet crank, but I fear putting in a $1800 crank and $400 rods, that not many peopple will want to buy it when i'm done<BR> <BR>I wonder how strong the stock crank is, and if it would be worth balanceing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Xtreme Fiero's (edited 10-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||2FAST4U||10-05-2000||02:00 AM||||Don't try using a V6 fuel pump on a duke - it will not work.<P>If you really want to do this kind of stuff, I've got a set of Crower billet rods already machined for a Duke.<BR>But then you'll need custom pistons to fit the bigger SBC pin size, I've got those also. JE forged pistons, 9.5:1 compression, 1/16-1/16-3/16 Total Seal rings, double spiro locks, tool steel wrist pins.<P>Also have Duke heads, ported, polished, flow matched on a Super Flow SF600 flow bench, bigger SS valves, titanium or aluminum retainers, appropriate springs, and roller rockers. <BR>Ported and matched intakes are also available. Manifold can be machined to accept bigger Holley TB without using spacer adapter.<P>You really don't need a billet crank. properly blueprinted and nitrided stock cranks are good to 7,000 RPMs, I've got these also.<P>I also have custom ground cams and other items for the duke and the V6 including performance short blocks and complete engines<P>If your interested, email me<P>See Ya<P>2fast4u||||reg||3
